        "original_id": "dde720a2-4926-5c04-a49d-b98bae105e15",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: J. L. C. Pompe van Meerdervoort\n- Places: Bruges, Brussels, Nagasaki, Japan\n- Roles: Dutch physician\n- Countries and States: United Kingdom of the Netherlands, Kingdom of the Netherlands\n- Historical Periods: Bakumatsu period\n\nFacts:\n- The United Kingdom of the Netherlands is the unofficial name for the Kingdom of the Netherlands as it existed from 1815 to 1830.\n- Johannes Lijdius Catharinus Pompe van Meerdervoort was born on 5 May 1829 in Bruges.\n- Johannes Lijdius Catharinus Pompe van Meerdervoort was a Dutch physician based at Nagasaki in Bakumatsu period Japan.\n- Johannes Lijdius Catharinus Pompe van Meerdervoort died on 7 October 1908 in Brussels.",
